   "text": {
    "L1": "This story is an unexpected adventure with a scooter.",
    "L2": "To retell it, put the main events in order.",
    "L3": "First, Dadaji parked the scooter near the village fair and went to buy jalebis.",
    "L4": "Then Chintu pressed the start button.",
    "L5": "Next, the scooter rolled down the slope.",
    "L6": "Finally, it stopped in a pile of hay.",
    "L7": "Use past-tense verbs because these events already happened.",
    "L8": "Some verbs add -ed: roll becomes rolled.",
    "L9": "But some verbs change shape: run becomes ran, and go becomes went.",
    "L10": "Dadaji came running because he was worried about Chintu.",
    "L11": "At the end, Dadaji shows care for Chintu's safety."
   },
